Sval: SessionStore says when a restore has set a tab's custom values

restoreTab sets a tab's custom values from the state it restores, so a tab
duplicateTab or setTabState copies arrives carrying its original's values,
Sval's node id among them. Nothing tells a listener at that moment:
SSTabRestoring fires only once restoreDocShellState resolves, by which time
other code can have read the copied id. Sval gives the copy its own node from
this event. It is dispatched at the end of restoreTab, after the method's
other events, as the method's own comment asks of anything external.

diff --git a/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs b/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
index c05c99d948..301c379fc1 100644
--- a/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
@@ -6667,6 +6667,12 @@ var SessionStoreInternal = {
     // while we wait for the messages to be processed.
     this.updateTabLabelAndIcon(tab, tabData);
 
+    // Tell listeners the tab's custom values are now tabData's, while
+    // nothing else has run since they were set.
+    let valuesEvent = window.document.createEvent("Events");
+    valuesEvent.initEvent("SSTabCustomValuesRestored", true, false);
+    tab.dispatchEvent(valuesEvent);
+
     // Decrease the busy state counter after we're done.
     this._setWindowStateReady(window);
   },
